    "core": 47
  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "If something that you're doing doesn't challenge you, then it doesn't change you.Spoiled by modern {civilization} , we easily {settle} into our daily routines.Yet we all need some {normal} stress in our lives, as the most rewarding experiences often lie beyond the familiar, waiting for {pioneers} to explore them.Think of comfort zones as a {cozy blanket} that keeps us warm but also {restricts} our {motions} .You can never see any improvement if you stick to it.The {willingness} to face {trials} is what successful people share as a common trait, whether they are a respected {gentleman} or {lady} , or a {badminton champion} .Challenge the {following limits} .It's essential to recognize that personal growth occurs when we dare to step into the {distant} unknown.",
      "cn": "如果你所做的事情对你来说没有挑战性，那么它就无法改变你。我们被现代 文明 宠坏了，很容易 安于 日常惯例。然而，我们在生活中都需要一些 正常的 压力，因为最有价值的经历常常存在于熟悉的事物之外，等待着 先驱 们去探索。可以把舒适区想象成一条 舒服的毯子 ，它让我们感到温暖，但也 限制 了我们的 行动 。如果你一直待在舒适区，你就永远看不到进步。 愿意 面对 考验 是成功人士的共同特点，无论他们是受人尊敬的 绅士 或 淑女 ，还是 羽毛球冠 军 。挑战 以下 这些 极限 吧。必须认识到，当我们敢于踏入 遥远的 未知领域时，个人成长才会发生。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Figure out what you're scared of and do it {continuously} .",
      "cn": "很多人一想到改变就 头晕目眩 ，这很正常。这种暂时的不适，与改变之后等待我们的 财富 相比，只是一个很小的 代价 。假设你是一名 推销员 ，你现在害怕 当面 与人交谈或打 电话 。与其 害怕 并认为自己会失败，不如每天至少花五分钟拿起电话拨打出去。也许有些人会挂断你的电话，但不要因此太过 失望 ！最终，你会直面恐惧，并说：“继续做吧，我不怕！”"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Many people feel {dizzy} at the thought of change, and that's perfectly natural.This temporary discomfort is a small {price} to pay for the {treasure} waiting on the other side.If you're a {salesman} , and you're scared of talking to people {personally} or over the {phone} now, instead of being {frightened} and thinking you'll fail, spend at least five minutes a day picking up the phone and make a call.Someone may hang up on you, but don't get too {disappointed} ! Eventually, you can look fear in the eye and say,“Go on.I'm not scared!”",
      "cn": "走出舒适区并不需要像攀登 塔楼 或成为 天文学家 那样 宏伟的 举动。确保这个爱好与你的 职业 无关；它应当有助于你放松身心、 缓解 压力。举几个例子，你可以学习一门新语言，如 德语 或 俄语 ，也可以尝试弹 吉他 等等。 除了 帮助你挑战自我之外，为爱好报一门课程可能还会为你带来额外的 收入 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Take a class for a hobby you've been wanting to develop.",
      "cn": "你不需要去 健身房 。在你家附近简单地跑九分钟就能给你带来意想不到的效果。运动不仅能帮你保持 正常 体重，还能让你对自己感觉 更好 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "The journey out of one's comfort zone doesn't require a {grand} gesture like climbing a {tower} or becoming an {astronomer} .Make sure this hobby is not linked to your {career} ; it should help you relax and {relieve} stress.Some examples might be learning a new language like {German} or {Russian} , trying to play the {guitar} and so on. {Apart} from helping you challenge yourself, taking a class for your hobby may also give you extra {income} .",
      "cn": "不要只局限于和同行的 旅伴 交流，试着和 服务人员建立联系 。你永远不知道他们会是怎样的人。现在就订张机 票 ， 飞 往一个陌生的目的地吧。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "Set {aside} at least {nine} minutes a day for physical exercise.",
      "cn": ""
    },
    {
      "num": "07",
      "en": "You don't need to go to the {gym} .A simple nine-minute run around your neighborhood can do wonders for you.Exercise can not only help you maintain your {regular} weight, but also make you feel {better} about yourself.",
      "cn": ""
    },
    {
      "num": "08",
      "en": "Travel and open yourself up to meeting new people.",
      "cn": ""
    },
    {
      "num": "09",
      "en": "Don't just limit yourself to your fellow {travelers} , and try to {connect} with the {service staff} .You never know what kind of people they're going to be.Book a {ticket} and take a {flight} to an unfamiliar destination right now.",
      "cn": ""
    }
  ],
